      "body": "Fixes #46661\n\nInternLM emits `<|action_start|>` and `<|plugin|>` as separate tokens. After the first streamed tool call, the detector currently clears the buffer when the next call's partial start marker arrives, so subsequent tool calls are dropped.\n\nKeep a suffix that can still become the next start marker while continuing to suppress already-emitted text. Add a CPU regression test using the token-by-token chunking from the issue.\n\nTests:\n- `python -m py_compile python/sglang/srt/function_call/internlm_detector.py test/registered/unit/function_call/test_internlm_detector.py`\n- Isolated parser regression reproduces two calls with tool indexes 0 and 1.\n- The focused pytest collection is blocked on this Windows host by SGLang's Linux-only `resource` dependency; CI should run the repository test in its supported environment.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40403658658](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40403658658)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40403658765](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40403658765)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40403658597](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40403658597)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
